>
>Seeing no way out anyway, I picked up one of the gold piles... and soon after
>a guard came and told me to drop the gold and follow him.  So I dropped the
>gold I had just picked up and went to follow him.
>
>But he told me to drop the gold immediately... but all the gold I was
>carrying was mine good and proper...
>
>so he killed me.
>
>How could I have escaped?

When a guard catches you in a vault, he doesn't know which gold is 
yours and which belongs there.  So he forces you to drop it all.
You could have dropped it all and then followed him out.

Also, your pick-axe may have gotten you out:

























When you get a message "the wall SEEMS too hard to dig in", this is 
different from the message "the wall IS too hard to dig in".  If
you get the SEEMS message, just keep digging and you'll eventually 
get through the wall. 
